  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>On the shores of Lac de Sainte-Croix, at Bauduen, PLAYA Location rents electric boats, pedal boats (with a slide or a sun canopy), kayaks, canoes and paddleboards. To go out with a dog, only the electric boats matter.</p>

      <h2>The dog rule depends on the boat</h2>
      <p>The official website is clear. The <strong>Lagon 55</strong> page (solar-powered, no licence needed, 10 people including 7 adults, 8 hours of battery, solar-panel roof that shades the deck, bathing ladder) says "dogs are allowed". The <strong>Scoop+</strong> page (7 people, stainless-steel sun canopy, picnic table) says "dogs are not allowed". Choose the Lagon 55 if your dog is coming aboard. On land, the website footer says "pets accepted on a leash". For the pedal boats, kayaks, canoes and paddleboards, the dog rule is not stated: ask before booking.</p>

      <h2>Lagon 55 prices and time slots</h2>
      <p>Prices shown on the official website: 2 hours €110, half-day of 4 hours (9am-1pm) €215, 6 hours €285, 8 hours (9am-5pm) €350. A reduced rate applies automatically in low season (1 April to 30 June and 1 September to 31 October, depending on opening dates). The 6- and 8-hour options allow a trip towards the Verdon gorges, but the site states that landing on the banks is forbidden, so your dog stays on board for the whole outing.</p>

      <h2>Hours and facilities</h2>
      <p>April, May and October: 10am-6pm, closed Tuesday and Wednesday. June and September: daily, 9am-6pm. July and August: daily, 9am-7pm, weather permitting. A refreshment bar (drinks, coffee, ice cream) and a shaded terrace with tables and chairs are on site. Payment by card, cash or ANCV holiday vouchers; several free car parks nearby. Booking is online, by phone or on site.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: book the Lagon 55 (not the Scoop+), bring a flotation vest for your dog, fresh water and a towel, and confirm by phone that your dog can board.</div>
      <p><strong>To check:</strong> the tourist office listing (updated May 2025) shows slightly different hours (daily in April) and does not mention the per-boat rule; the operator's own website prevails.</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Lac de Sainte-Croix and the entrance to the Verdon gorges form the setting of the trip. The village of Bauduen, about 2 km away according to the tourist office, has a Romanesque church (Saint-Pierre-et-Saint-Paul), 15th-century ramparts and an old oil mill.</p>
